[{"answer":"OK, so what I'd like you to do now is to talk to your partner about your presentations on urban planning.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/1.mp3"},{"answer":"You should have done most of the reading now, so I'd like you to share your ideas,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/2.mp3"},{"answer":"and talk about the structure of your presentation and what you need to do next.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/3.mp3"},{"answer":"OK Rob.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/4.mp3"},{"answer":"I'm glad we chose quite a specific topic - cities built next to the sea.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/5.mp3"},{"answer":"It made it much easier to find relevant information.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/6.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah. And cities are growing so quickly -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/7.mp3"},{"answer":"I mean, we know that more than half the world's population lives in cities now.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/8.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah, though that's all cities, not just ones on the coast.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/9.mp3"},{"answer":"But most of the biggest cities are actually built by the sea.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/10.mp3"},{"answer":"I'd not realised that before.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/11.mp3"},{"answer":"Nor me.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/12.mp3"},{"answer":"And what's more, a lot of them are built at places where rivers come out into the sea.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/13.mp3"},{"answer":"But apparently this can be a problem.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/14.mp3"},{"answer":"Why?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/15.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, as the city expands,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/16.mp3"},{"answer":"agriculture and industry tend to spread further inland along the rivers,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/17.mp3"},{"answer":"and so agriculture moves even further inland up the river.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/18.mp3"},{"answer":"That's not necessarily a problem,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/19.mp3"},{"answer":"except it means more and more pollutants are discharged into the rivers.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/20-2024-11-04-16-31-15.mp3"},{"answer":"So these are brought downstream to the cities?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/21.mp3"},{"answer":"Right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/22.mp3"},{"answer":"Did you read that article about Miami, on the east coast of the USA?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/23.mp3"},{"answer":"No.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/24.mp3"},{"answer":"Well, apparently back in the 1950s,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/25.mp3"},{"answer":"they built channels to drain away the water in case of flooding.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Sounds sensible.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/27.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah, they spent quite a lot of money on them.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/28.mp3"},{"answer":"But what they didn't take into account was global warming.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/29.mp3"},{"answer":"So they built the drainage channels too close to sea level,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/30.mp3"},{"answer":"and now sea levels are rising, they're more or less useless.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/31-2024-11-04-16-54-49.mp3"},{"answer":"If there's a lot of rain, the water can't run away, there's nowhere for it to go.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/32.mp3"},{"answer":"The whole design was faulty.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/33.mp3"},{"answer":"So what are the authorities doing about it now?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/34.mp3"},{"answer":"I don't know.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/35.mp3"},{"answer":"I did read that they're aiming to stop disposing of waste water into the ocean over the next ten years.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/36.mp3"},{"answer":"But that won't help with flood prevention now, will it?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/37.mp3"},{"answer":"No. Really they just need to find the money for something to replace the drainage channels,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/38.mp3"},{"answer":"in order to protect against flooding now.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/39.mp3"},{"answer":"But in the long term they need to consider the whole ecosystem.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/40.mp3"},{"answer":"Right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/41.mp3"},{"answer":"Really, though, coastal cities can't deal with their problems on their own, can they?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/42.mp3"},{"answer":"I mean, they've got to start acting together at an international level instead of just doing their own thing.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/43.mp3"},{"answer":"Absolutely.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/44.mp3"},{"answer":"The thing is, everyone knows what the problems are","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/45.mp3"},{"answer":"and environmentalists have a pretty good idea of what we should be doing about them,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/46-2024-11-04-17-01-23.mp3"},{"answer":"so they should be able to work together to some extent.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/47.mp3"},{"answer":"But it's going to be a long time before countries come to a decision on what principles they're prepared to abide by.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/48.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah, if they ever do.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/49.mp3"},{"answer":"So I think we've probably got enough for our presentation.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/50.mp3"},{"answer":"It's only fifteen minutes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/51.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/52.mp3"},{"answer":"So I suppose we'll begin with some general historical background","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/53.mp3"},{"answer":"about why coastal cities were established.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/54.mp3"},{"answer":"But we don't want to spend too long on that,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/55.mp3"},{"answer":"the other students will already know a bit about it.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/56.mp3"},{"answer":"It's all to do with communications and so on.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/57.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/58.mp3"},{"answer":"We should mention some geographical factors,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/59.mp3"},{"answer":"things like wetlands and river estuaries and coastal erosion and so on.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/60.mp3"},{"answer":"We could have some maps of different cities with these features marked.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/61.mp3"},{"answer":"On a handout you mean?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/62.mp3"},{"answer":"Or some slides everyone can see?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/63.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah, that'd be better.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/64.mp3"},{"answer":"It'd be good to go into past mistakes in a bit more detail.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/65.mp3"},{"answer":"Did you read that case study of the problems there were in New Orleans with flooding a few years ago?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/66.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, We could use that as the basis for that part of the talk.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/67.mp3"},{"answer":"I don't think the other students will have read it,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/68.mp3"},{"answer":"but they'll remember hearing about the flooding at the time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/69.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/70.mp3"},{"answer":"So that's probably enough background.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/71.mp3"},{"answer":"So then we'll go on to talk about what action's being taken to deal with the problems of coastal cities.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/72.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/73.mp3"},{"answer":"What else do we need to talk about?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/74.mp3"},{"answer":"Maybe something on future risks, looking more at the long term, if populations continue to grow.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/75.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/76.mp3"},{"answer":"We'll need to do a bit of work there,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/77.mp3"},{"answer":"I haven't got much information, have you?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/78.mp3"},{"answer":"No. We'll need to look at some websites.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/79.mp3"},{"answer":"Shouldn't take too long.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/80.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/81.mp3"},{"answer":"And I think we should end by talking about international implications.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/82.mp3"},{"answer":"Maybe we could ask people in the audience.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/83.mp3"},{"answer":"We've got people from quite a lot of different places.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/84.mp3"},{"answer":"That'd be interesting, if we have time, yes.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/85.mp3"},{"answer":"So now...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-14-test-1-part-3-2023-01-26-23-55-43/86.mp3"}]
